## 4. Historical Data for Prediction

The historical traffic endpoint is:

GET /traffic/history/{road_id}

It provides time-series traffic information for a particular road.

### Data Fields

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| `reading_id` | Unique identifier of the traffic reading |
| `road_id` | Identifier of the road |
| `sensor_id` | Identifier of the traffic sensor |
| `timestamp` | Time when the traffic reading was recorded |
| `vehicle_count` | Number of vehicles detected |
| `density` | Traffic density between 0 and 1 |
| `congestion_level` | Current congestion category |

### Example

```json
{
    "reading_id": 101,
    "road_id": 1,
    "sensor_id": 5,
    "timestamp": "2026-09-01T10:30:00",
    "vehicle_count": 75,
    "density": 0.63,
    "congestion_level": "MEDIUM"
}